				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">Time passes slow like the observation of a glowing orange ember clinging to burning life as it drifts it's way towards the ceiling. This is much the same for those gathered within the walls of the Kindred Spirits. Life moves slowly for those within as the people slowly mill about, trading stories with others. Sharing drink with those friends who have not been seen in a dragon's age.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
When suddenly the door to the tavern bursts open with such violence, that the wind kicked up from the swing blows out the candles adorning the closest tables to the door as a young elf wearing soft purple robes stands in the doorway panting, totally out of breath but a big smile across his weary face.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;It has happened! This day is a glorious day for those upon the sides of light! Justice has been served for those who have fallen! It was brought by a lizard who stood before the might of Freeport! Listen close as I proclaim this wonderful news!&quot; He says as he slowly walks into the tavern his eyes darting this way and that as he seeks the attention of the entire tavern.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Freedom has been brought to Freeport by this being... This creature who stood as a beacon of light in a world of darkness. One who has gone against the bias and shown that good still stands its ground against evils in this land! This creature... This samurai has defeated the Freeport Militia!&quot; He exclaims as he rests himself against the bar. &quot;I had seen it with my own eyes!&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He pauses for a moment to catch his breath before deciding to continue. Indalis puts a glass of water before him to quench the thirst of running so hard.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;It was incredible I tell you! One being stood at the outskirts of the city his swords in hand, his armor shone bright like the sun upon a crystaline lake, he just stood there, defiant against the bias' of the city. His kind oh so distrusted there... One would never have thought an Iksar would do this.&quot; he sipped at the water to regain his voice which was breaking slightly from his fevered run.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;I watched as he slowly raised his sword to the air, lifting it high so all could see, one foot forward the other back as he looked up to the sky and then towards the front gates of western freeport, he then spoke with a determination that I have not seen since the freeport militia took over the city so long ago. 'Listen closely Sir Lucan De'lere! I have come to find you! I have come to bring justice in the name of Mithaniel Marr for the deaths of all those paladins who have come before me and who have died by your hand! I have come to bring peace back to this city you rule over with an iron fist! So listen closely! It is time to make peace with this mortal coil for I am comming for you! First your guards... They will fall one by one to my blade, and then as they fall you shall feel the sting of pain as the paladins did when you betrayed them. For every single one that has died I shall remove one of your guards until none are left but you and I!' He then lowered his blade to point towards the front gates and began walking forward... The guards all looked at each other as the saw his radiant form slowly come into view as he walked.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The elf smiled ever so brightly as he told the story of what he had seen, almost like a young elf running through the treetops of Kelethin. He was giddy with happiness.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;I followed him from the safty of distance as I saw one of the guards lower their helm to regard him and begin running towards him saying that scum like him were not welcome in Freeport. By the gods themselves this warrior was faster than even those I had heard of being enchanted by the spells of the most powerful of my discipline. It was like his blade never left it's position. I merely blinked and he was just walking past the guard who had stood frozen in a lunge. all I heard was the sound of this strange warrior replacing his sword within the scabbard on his hip. and the guard he past his gurgled once as blood began to pour from just under his helm and he fell over... Dead.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He chuckled, &quot;I had thought this creature was crazy when he started his walk and thought that the first would have killed him and that would have been the end of it... But no, he had killed one so easily that my heart began to pound, feeling the adrenaline pumping through my veins as if I had just cast a spell. He just continued to walk forward towards the gates one clawed green hand upon the hilt... The other upon the scabbard, he walked as two more guards from the gates ran at him weapons drawn. The first never got a chance to strike as the other lunged at the lizard's side, but neither would score a strike as the lizard stepped forward into the first guar his right hand drawing foward the hilt of his blade driving it into the forhead of the first snapping his head back with such sharpness that all I heard was the distinguishing SNAP! of this neck breaking and him cartwheeling away from the warrior. The other missed his mark completely as his blade passed behind the back of him. I watched him turn sharply his tail struck soundly into the back of the second guard's lead leg causing him to over-extend his stride bringing him down to a knee and with one decisive swing the 'samurai' as he called himself spun his blade's edge never seeming to touch the man's body at all. It came away from the guard clean, no blood, I thought he had missed his mark until I watched the head of the guard topple from his shoulders in a spray of crimson lifeforce.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The elf sighed for a second in blissful memory, taking a long draw from his glass of water before placing it back down upon the bartop and continuing.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;He then spoke again as I watched from my hiding place, 'Three have fallen Lucan! Your guards are not trainned to defeat a samurai! Their skills are sloppy and they move too slowly, Mithaniel Marr is with me this day and I am comming for you! Your Time in this land grows short! I am tired of hearing of you slaughtering those who seek to protect the good in this land... And YOU of all people once a paladin of Marr yourself! Have turned your back from your bretheren! Saying that YOU! are the true hand of Marr! For your sins against yours, and my faith. It is time to pay the piper.' He walked on as if he had never broken stride his sword moving with the alacrity of flowing water never once breaking momentum as he was attacked, again and again, but like a plow he kept moving forward towards the guardhouse where Lucan De'Lere lay his head. It was like a dream, people scattered from their houses, Paladins and priests alike ran from their spots to see what was going on, Even Valeron Dushire came out running at the thought that one person would be able to do what the entire paladin legion could not.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He just raised his arms and just passed them over the entranced crowd to emphasize the amount of people who had witnessed this.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;All watched as he walked calmly, as if death had no longer concerned him, nothing was stopping him, it was like Mithaniel Marr himself had infused him with the power of his avatar to defeat this scourge who had for so long been a cancer upon these lands. He stood before the door to the gatehouse and spoke once more, bleeding from would that had been caused by the blades of so many guards, I figure about fifteen to twenty guards all of elitist skill lay around him not a single one of them still breathing.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Then he pointed to the door as it swung open letting another into the room, &quot;It was like that, the door swung open, and just as it did the sounds of mystical prayers could be heard being spoken. A powerful divine spell indeed. I could tell by the strain it put upon a single guard who walked out. Brother Jentry, Lucan's healing sink. But the words were cut short as the lizard drew up a misty almost non existant bow and let fly a single silvery arrow... It arced with incredible speed drawing behind it a single beam of pure white energy, the missle flew true, penitrating the helm the dark cleric wore like it was nothing more than made of parchmount. It must have killed him instantly as the weapon lifted the cleric off the ground sending him rocketing backwards and pinned him like a trainning dummy to the now closed door behind him.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Then slowly the door opened again as a single figure stepped out, brandishing two finely crafted longswords and approached the lizard standing there. He walked ever so slowly forward and stopped about a blade's distance from the samurai. You know I guess Lucan knew it was his time because he slowly bowed to the samurai who in turn did the same, and he spoke quietly, 'I am Rithnok Tatsukao Flamespewer. Samurai to the Emperor Ryoko Musashi of Edo Japan, and I have come to challenge you Sir Lucan De'lere. Do you in honour accept this challenge?' he asked, Sir Lucan just bowed his head and set himself within his fighting stance preparing to fight. The Iksarian Samurai did the same, and there he stood like a pillar of faith, The souls of all those warriors who had died before him standing behind him, almost like they were using him as a vessel to release their vengaence upon those who had killed them in cold blood.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The elf just stood up and began to mimic the battle as he saw it, &quot;It was a blur of motion, the samurai began to fight, his blade moving like a willow branch so fast, so accurate. But it was not so easy to kill Lucan as it was his guards. The battle raged for hours, each of them trading blows in a symphony of steel. But it would seem as naught. Lucan was wearing the samurai down. his attacks were fast, scoring only little strikes but with the wounding of the samurai through his earlier combats they were beginning to take their toll, when the samurai finally said, 'It may be that on this day I meet my end Lucan, but if I do I know that in my soul I fought for all those before me, and even if I fail, I know that I will fail fighting for what I believe is right... Fighting to avenge all those fatherless sons and daughters, those wives who have lost their husands, all those who have ever lost anyone to your militia and your guards shall be avenged even in my death!' And it was with that both warriors so weary from the combat, that sir Lucan brought both his weapons forward in a final thrust. I watched in horror as they pierced the flesh of the samurai parting it like it was the pages of a spellbook.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He sighed and hung his head at this point, and then raised it with a smile, &quot;If I had not seen this with eyes of my own I would swear it was not true, but I did, a small pillar of light lanced down from the heavens above striking the ground beside the samurai revealing the form of a gnome in green robes who just stood there quietly. everyone stepped back except the paladins and priests, who just kneeled and began to pray. I do not know exactly what was going on myself but I watched as the samurai stared at Lucan with determination in his eyes. The gnome beside him just looked to the lizard and smiled speaking quietly, 'Worry not young one, Mithaniel Marr blesses you this day. For you stand against the darkness alone knowing that you might die, but you will not, this is not your time.' and with that he touched the samurai. The lizard then dropped his weapon, and gripped both blades that had been stuck in his body the blades both bit deeply into his hands as red blood began to flow, he showed no emotion as he slowly with a long drawn exhale pulled the blades out from his body, the mortal wounds he had recieved slowly closing as he did, horror washed over Lucan's eyes which could be seen through his helm. as the blades left his body the samurai slowly stood up and smiled, 'This is the day your tyrinical rule comes to an end fallen paladin.' was all that he said as with a shrp motion his hands came off the blades and struck lucan's elbows with such force that the former paladin's arms buckled drawing his blades inside his guard. The Samurai gripped the knight's wrists and guiding the now uncontrolled blades into the soft fleshy part of his belly both blades piercing into the tender skin to stop with a quiet ring against his back armor as they passed right through his body, he stared at the gnome in disbelief. The gnome then stepped forward as Lucan dropped to his knees, he kissed him upon the helm and only said, 'Sleep now my misguided warrior, your sins have been forgiven. You have paid for them in full.'&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The elf cheered happily at this and raised his glass, &quot;It was then that the gnome turned and faced the samurai and smiles to him who just kneeled and bowed his head, 'Listen well young one, on this day, you have returned a lost sheep to my arms and for that I shall grant you one wish, a wish which will fulfill an oath you made to one of my own so long ago in your journies here dragon. I had been asked to watch over you to keep you from the eyes of other dragonslayers, but I have seen here this day that you have no need of being protected and that I can only hope that all will see you with the same love and honour that I see you with. and so from this day forth all in the lands of Norrath shall know you as, &quot;Rithnok Tatsukao Flamespewer The Samurai of Norrath.&quot; now rest well and know that this city shall always call you, it's saviour.' The samurai smiled and stood up he bowed to the gnome and spoke back, 'M'lord, I came here not seeking reward, nor seeking glory but simply to avenge the loss of those who had always been so kind to me. It was time for his reign to end, now I turn over the city to the hand of those who shall rule with peace and protect those who seek a haven from the forces of Innoruk and Cazic-Thule. Let the Preists and Paladins of Marr rule with love and compassion. But for me, my work is not yet done and there are many more who shall need to find honour in this world... I just hope I can do my part to the best of my ability so no other place shall find the rule of any more Lucans.' he then turned and bowed to Valeron and smiled to him, 'Rule well m'lord.' was all he said as he picked up his strange curved blade and walked towards the direction of the Eastern Commonlands.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The elf just smiled and put down his now empty glass, &quot;This was the last I had seen of this Iksar, this Samurai, this... Saviour. All I remember hearing at this point was a strong voice in my mind which had said, 'Mithaniel Marr has granted a wish upon this day!' and with that the gnome had disappeared and so had the samurai. But let it be known that upon this day the City of Freeport is now free from the darkness of the corrupt freeport militia and for another thousand years let it stand as the first great victory in the wars against the darkness! Cheers!&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
He raises his glass to the air for all to see, &quot;Cheers to the Samurai of Norrath! and may Mithaniel Marr guide him true in his endevors across these lands, and Cheers to Felwithe for calling him friend, and Cheers to the Concordant Angelis for calling him ally! For he truely is a Guardian of Honour!&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Rithnok Tatsukao Flamespewer
