		<td class="row2" width="100%" height="28" valign="top"><table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0">
			<tr>
				<td width="100%"><a href="viewtopic.php?p=15898&amp;sid=3ec44e9b483f47e22a412dc9eb10dc54#15898"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/icon_minipost.gif" width="12" height="9" alt="Post" title="Post" border="0" /></a><span class="postdetails">Posted: Tue Sep 03, 2002 6:31 pm<span class="gen">&nbsp;</span>&nbsp; &nbsp;Post subject: </span></td>
				<td valign="top" align="right" nowrap="nowrap"><a href="posting.php?mode=quote&amp;p=15898&amp;sid=3ec44e9b483f47e22a412dc9eb10dc54"><img src="templates/Chronicles/images/lang_english/icon_quote.gif" alt="Reply with quote" title="Reply with quote" border="0" /></a>   </td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><hr /></td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td colspan="2"><span class="postbody">While waiting for an answer (patient as always), Darven sits at the bar with his cup in hand. 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
A young high elf walks up, bowing quite formally to the shaman, a bundle of papers in hand. &quot;M'Lord, the head librarian has sent these to you&quot; the young man pipes up. Darven looks about, trying to discover who the young elf speaks to. Realizing he is the one the elf speaks to, he suddenly busts into racous laughter.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Seeing the surprised and almost frightened look upon the young elf's face, the shaman claps him soundly on the shoulder, smiling. The strike nearly knocks the little elf over, and he yelps as he grabs at the papers in his hand. Darven, smiling still, holds him on his feet with one large hand, placed carefully to the back of the elf's neck.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;Well now boyo, I doan be a Lord, but I do appreciate yer bringin' me these!&quot;He takes the papers from the high elf, and grins happily as he looks them over. &quot;Jest wot I was hopin' for&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The high elf blanches at the sound of Darven's laughter, a look of bewilderment on his face. His voice stammers slightly, one long finger extended to point at the papers &quot;M-m-master said to be careful with those. We don't have th-th-that many copies left&quot; 
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Darven nods, and settles the papers down on the bar top as if they were made of the thinnest ice. &quot;Aye, boyo, I'll be careful, ye've got m' Word on tha'.&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
The young man stands there for a moment more, uncertain of what to do then. He decides that he has done all that he can to protect his master's writings, and takes his leave.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
Darven settles the papers down a bit, smoothing out the edges with his large hand. His touch is gentle, and he holds his bottom lip in his teeth as he touches the paper. He is the picture of concentration as he begins to read, speaking the words softly to himself.
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
&quot;The..... history of... Caelyn, son of Danval... Goblinkiller...&quot;
<br />

<br />

<br />

<br />
 
<br />
Darven Twopaws 
<br />
 Shaman<i></i></span><span class="gentblsmall"></span></td>
